<%# Search, opened over the page.

    brgen carried search twice — a link in the left nav and a field in the right
    widgets rail — and both rails are gone. This replaces them and costs no
    permanent chrome: a glyph beside the wordmark, "/" for a reader and Cmd-K
    for an operator.

    The trigger is a real button and the shortcuts are an accelerator on top of
    it, never the only way in. The form is shared/live_search_form, the same one
    the posts and communities indexes use, so results stream here through the
    machinery that already exists rather than a second search path. %>
<div class="search_palette" data-controller="search-palette">
  <button type="button"
          class="search_palette_trigger"
          data-action="click->search-palette#open"
          aria-label="<%= t("nav.search") %>"
          aria-keyshortcuts="/ Meta+K">
    <%= icon :search, size: 22 %>
  </button>

  <%# aria-modal with a label, so a screen reader is told this is a layer over
      the page rather than more of it. Escape and focus return live in the
      controller. %>
  <div class="search_palette_overlay"
       role="dialog"
       aria-modal="true"
       aria-label="<%= t("nav.search") %>"
       data-action="click->search-palette#backdrop">
    <div class="search_palette_panel" data-search-palette-target="panel">
      <%= render "shared/live_search_form",
                 url: main_app.global_search_path,
                 query: params[:q],
                 placeholder: t("nav.search_placeholder"),
                 label: t("nav.search"),
                 show_submit: false,
                 show_suggestions: false %>
      <%# Where the Turbo Stream lands. The shared form's input already names
          this id in aria-controls. %>
      <div id="live_search_results" class="search_palette_results" aria-live="polite"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
